// The groundcover package: lush, lived-in ground from rules. A program
// reaches it with 'import groundcover', and gets (full account: types.cone's
// header, and Design\groundcover.md):
//
// - CoverType (types.cone), a description of one kind of cover as DATA: what
//   it is drawn as (grass tufts that bend in the wind, flowers, ground-hugging
//   patches such as moss, fallen leaves, or any registered mesh: ferns, pebbles,
//   fallen branches, shrubs), how dense, which ground it likes (a window on each
//   of eight signals), how it clumps, its size, colour and wind, how far it is
//   drawn and how it thins with distance, and which other types it gives way to.
// - GroundMaps (maps.cone), the eight signals over a patch of ground (height,
//   slope, moisture, sun exposure, distance to a path, to water, canopy, distance to
//   an object), with helpers that derive slope, exposure and moisture and rasterise
//   paths, streams, boulders and tree crowns into them.
// - The rules on the CPU (place.cone): the score of a type at a point, the
//   instances of a cell, a ring, and the far-field colour baked from the same rules.
//   cover.slang holds the same arithmetic for the GPU.
// - CoverRenderer (renderer.cone), which places the cover the camera needs by
//   compute shaders every frame (generate.slang) and draws it with indirect draws
//   (draw.slang) into render's HDR frame after the opaque scene.
//
// A frame, with render's Renderer (keeping its depth: 'renderer.keepDepth = true'):
//
//   mut cover = CoverRenderer.create(&mut device, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA16_FLOAT, TEXTURE_FORMAT_DEPTH32_FLOAT);
//   imm fern = cover.addMesh(&fernMesh);                                  // once, before 'build'
//   cover.build(&mut device, &types, &maps);                              // once, or when the ground changes
//   ...
//   renderer.render(&mut device, &mut encoder, &post.hdr, &depth, &camera, &light, &list);
//   cover.render(&mut device, &mut encoder, &post.hdr, &depth, &camera, &environment);
//   post.apply(&mut encoder, &target);
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   types.cone      CoverType, Window, Interaction, the signals, validation
//   maps.cone       GroundMaps, the derivations and rasterisers
//   place.cone      the rules on the CPU, the far field
//   renderer.cone   CoverRenderer; generate.slang's and draw.slang's SPIR-V
//
// and its shaders, Slang: generate (the placement kernels), draw (every kind's
// geometry and light) and the module cover (the rules) they import, which imports
// the noise package's.
//
// DETERMINISM. Where cover stands is a pure function of the types, the maps and
// the lattice cell (hashes of integers, the noise package's PCG): the same
// ground gives the same meadow, and a cell is placed the same whichever way the
// camera came. The hashes and counts are integers, the same everywhere; positions
// use sin, cos, log and square roots, which a GPU computes to looser bounds than
// the CPU, so the GPU's instance is close to the CPU's, not identical (the
// parity test measures how close).

mod groundcover;

import libc;
import stdio use *;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import mesh;
import noise use pcg, pcg4d, toUnit, UVec4;
import gpu use *;
import render use Camera, Light;
